**Flowchart: Adult Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA) Management (Simplified Overview)**

**(Disclaimer: This is a simplified reference flowchart for educational purposes. Always follow institutional protocols and exercise clinical judgment. This is not a substitute for comprehensive DKA guidelines. Specific values (e.g., fluid rates, insulin doses, K+ thresholds) may vary based on institutional protocols and patient-specific factors.)**

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Initial Assessment & Diagnosis] --> B{Initial Labs};
    B --> C[Fluid Resuscitation];
    C --> D{Check K+};
    D -- K+ > 3.3 mEq/L --> E[Start IV Insulin Infusion];
    D -- K+ <= 3.3 mEq/L --> F[Hold Insulin, Replace K+];
    F --> D;
    E --> G[Electrolyte Monitoring & Correction];
    G --> H{Monitor Glucose & Ketones};
    H --> I{Anion Gap Resolution?};
    I -- Yes --> J[Transition to Subcutaneous Insulin];
    I -- No --> G;
    J --> K[Overlap SC/IV Insulin];
    K --> L[Discontinue IV Insulin];
    L --> M[Patient Education & Discharge Planning];

    subgraph Initial Steps
        A
        B
        C
        D
        E
    end

    subgraph Ongoing Management
        G
        H
        I
    end

    subgraph Transition Phase
        J
        K
        L
        M
    end

    %% Details for each step (can be expanded)
    B -- Labs --> B1[BMP (Na, K, Cl, HCO3, BUN, Cr), Glucose, Beta-Hydroxybutyrate (BHB), ABG/VBG, CBC, Urinalysis];
    C -- Fluids --> C1[0.9% NaCl initially (e.g., 1-1.5L/hr), then adjust based on corrected Na & hydration status];
    E -- Insulin --> E1[IV Insulin Infusion (e.g., 0.1 U/kg/hr)];
    F -- K+ Replacement --> F1[Replace K+ aggressively (e.g., 20-30 mEq/hr) to maintain > 3.3 mEq/L before starting insulin];
    G -- Electrolytes --> G1[Monitor K+ frequently (q2-4h), replace as needed. Monitor Phos, Mg];
    H -- Monitoring --> H1[Monitor Glucose q1-2h, BHB q2-4h, Anion Gap];
    J -- Transition --> J1[Start SC Insulin (e.g., basal-bolus) when glucose < 200-250 mg/dL, anion gap closing, patient stable];
    K -- Overlap --> K1[Overlap IV & SC Insulin for 1-2 hours];
    L -- Discontinue --> L1[Stop IV Insulin once SC Insulin is effective & patient tolerating PO];
